Goodness me, no - most NetHack characters die to infant mortality, so get
the benefit from the wishes early. Wish for speed boots and find a pair
round the next corner - who cares? You've still got speed boots. Don't
wish for them and die because you couldn't run away - game over.

The OP has 4 or 5 wishes to come, depending on whether or not the wand
started 0:2 or 0:3. Now I'm not saying not to save a few wishes, but burn
a few as well. Speed boots for sure, but also a bag of holding. In
particular, if you save all the wishes and then the charging scrolls get
destroyed by a fire effect, you're going to look very silly.

If the wand was 0:3 I would definitely wish for a crunch damage artifact
(_not_ Magicbane - it's easy to get, already got MR, and for all that it's
nice, you also want something to hack up monsters quickly) and if it was
0:2 I would still consider it. The disadvantage if the wand is 0:2 is then
you only have the wrested wish in reserve, and you can't use that quickly
in response to an emergency.
